<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Ryukyu Islands, 2022</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Ryukyu Islands, 2022&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Al "Beirutdude" Sandrik&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;The Time Is: 4 April, 2022, 04:00 Zulu/12:00 Okinawa Time&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;First Island Chain/Ryukyu/Senkaku Islands&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Playable as PRC/PLAN/PLAAF Only&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;48 Hours Duration&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;(This is the prelude Scenario to "To Kill the Queen, 2022")&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;PLEASE read all the "Notes" &lt;U&gt;&lt;EM&gt;Really, please read them!&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/U&gt; Just saying…&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Background: &lt;/STRONG&gt;Chinese President Xi Jinping placed great emphasis in regaining the "lost Providence" of Taiwan during his Presidency, late in 2021 he was diagnosed with Stage Four cancer accelerating his timetable. Further exacerbating the situation, the Japanese Self Defense Forces had been garrisoning the outer islands of the Ryukyu’s chain and greatly increasing the radar capabilities of the islands. In 2019 new radars were placed on the western most island of the Yaeyama islands, Yonaguri Island. Other garrisons were built on the Miyako Islands and on Okinoerabujima Island. Each of these were about a battalion in strength. While they weren’t strong enough to stand against a determined PLAN invasion, they could turn the effort into a bloody fight. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In order to make the conquest of the Lost Providence easier and to ensure PLAN submarines and surface units had ready access to the open Pacific through the choke points, it was determined that first the southern Ryukyu Islands must be taken. As planning continued mission creep set in as some argued that most of the smaller islands in the Okinawan Island chain, including LeShima Island should also be taken to isolate the Japanese and American position on Okinawa.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Of course, the diplomats argued that any invasion of the islands would be seen as naked aggression until, retired Major General Luo Yuan, raised the territorial question of the Ryukyu’s status, saying the Ryukyus had started paying tribute to China in 1372, half a millennium before they were seized by Japan. As proof he presented a paper by two Chinese academics laying the case for the islands actually being Chinese territory. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;After great debate the invasion date was set for sunrise April 5th, 2022…&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Mission: &lt;/STRONG&gt;You have fourteen possible targets in the Ryukyu’s chain and Okinawa is not one of them (&lt;B&gt;&lt;I&gt;&lt;U&gt;yet&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/I&gt;&lt;/U&gt;, possible future scenario). You have been directed to take the Yaeyama and Miyoko Islands (all of the islands south of Okinawa) to facilitate future operations against Taiwan. You may use any means, short of nuclear weapons, to suppress American and Japanese resistance from Okinawa, the Ryukyus and any naval vessels. President Xi and the Central Committee have expressly forbidden any direct attacks on the Japanese Home Islands, to reduce the possibly of the war spinning out of control, unless there is a direct attack on the PRC homeland. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Notes: &lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This is a HUGE sceanrio nd may slow down when missiles are launched. Event without them it slows down significantly at times. Save early-save often! Make sure autosave is on (just saying). &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Please ensure that "Pop Up" messages are enabled.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Taiwan and South Korea try to sit this one out. USAF agrees not to use bases in the ROK.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This is an amphibious/cargo operation scenario, so you only gain points by taking the islands and more significantly their airports. To do so your amphibious forces (landed ground units) must remain inside the objective’s target area for one hour. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;I have set objective areas and suggested landing areas. They are locked reference points. DO NOT DELETE THEM! I have highlighted them at the beginning of the scenario, turn that off as you please, but don’t unlock and/or delete them.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;When you seize and airport/objective (Camp Yonaguri) it changes sides and you can use the airport. I didn’t have radar units, etc. change sides as they crew had better have rendered them unusable prior to their capture. For that reason it is bad idea to attack the airports outside of Okinawa itself.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=red&gt;EXTREMELY IMPORTANT:&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt; Cargo Operations, it is suggested you take as much control of the cargo operations, and especially the unloading cargo, as possible! Many of these islands have permanent wetlands on/surrounding them (which ground units bog down in). This is especially true for the smaller islands and the airport areas which seem to have been built on reclaimed wetlands! Try to land units in areas that go directly from Water to Grasslands, Croplands, Forest and Urban areas. Avoid Wetlands and Land-Water areas! &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;HINT: You might want to turn on the Land Cover map when planning and conducting landing ops. Run the cursor over the area and watch for Permanent Wetlands and Land-Water and avoid them!!!!!!!&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;HINT: LSTs land the APCs (and can troops) directly on the beaches and I have found it is best to break up the LST amphibious groups before landing with each LST individually landing its forces on islands near objectives with the corvettes covering them. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;On some islands I have suggested landing areas (as your planners would have done for you in real life)&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;On other islands it is almost hopeless and I have set the objective area to the entire island so you can land and gain the VPs even if your units bog down. Remember your LPDs and your LHD have heliborne forces and these islands might be good objectives for them (hint). &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Airborne forces have been reserved for future operations.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;You only have one load out of SRBMs/MRBMs as they are also being reserved for future operations (honestly we need missile loadouts with several hour load times to represent TEL reloads, otherwise I’d have to provide new missile units to represent reloads and this scenario was already too complicated).&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;I have loaded the aircraft as the large number of H-6s have a 20-hour loadout and they play such a key role. If you change the load outs, I suggest you do it in the Scenario Editor. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The JMSDF DDH Izumo has completed its refit and has F-35B’s aboard (so is it a CV? CVL? Now?). The pilots have recently been trained by the USMC which just completed orientation on Izumo themselves. JS Kaga is still in refit for this scenario. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Pound the bases on Okinawa with everything you can to suppress them, especially your SRBMs/IRBMs.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Ports: You have vessels in ports which can deploy so don’t forget them! Any vessel with a 30-day ready time is in maintenance status (like an aircraft at an airbase). &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;For the most part the Japanese Home Islands as single unit airbases to reduce the number of units, so please don’t attack the Home Islands. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;There is a possibility the JSDF/USAF (Allies) might strike first as your units come closer to the Ryukyus. This is especially true if you stumble into an exclusion zone. Stay in the dead center of any choke points if transiting them! &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;I have set some ASW and AEW missions on the Carrier Shendong, just suggestions do as you please. I just figured they would be present at this point in the scenario. As Allied AAW aircraft aren’t close to the CSG yet I figured you can set the AAW missions. There may be submarines close to her at the beginning. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Scoring: &lt;/STRONG&gt;0 points = Disaster and 6,000 a Triumph&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;　&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Built under C:MO Build 1147.14 Database DB3000 v487&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;.INI and Delta Files are provided for deep rebuilds.&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=""&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Al "BeirutDude" Sandrik (ex-Beachinnole)&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Al.Sandrik@gmail.com&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
